From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:35:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 140/143] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=private_memory, a
 private-storage memory type

Re-port of the private_memory patch of c8c6016 (reverted in c17946c)
onto 0019's typeless usage v2, 0119's memory priority, 0128-0135's
command BOs and 0129's residency commits, so that private storage can
be measured together with compressible usage, which it never was: the
2026-10-08 run had the old 0x15 usage, so it tested nothing about
lossless compression.

With the flag, KosmicKrisp lists a second memory type, DEVICE_LOCAL
only, before its host-visible one. Its memory is an MTLHeapTypePlacement
heap with MTLResourceStorageModePrivate and no buffer over the whole
heap (no CPU mapping, gpu and cpu unset); every other allocation stays
a shared-storage heap as now, and a heap Metal refuses still retries
once after a residency removal commit (0129).

- DXVK, vkd3d-proton and the WSI take the lowest memory type that fits
  the flags they ask for, so what they ask for as DEVICE_LOCAL without
  HOST_VISIBLE lands in the new type; what they map they ask for as
  HOST_VISIBLE and still get the host-visible type.
- Images that cannot be private (linear: buffer-backed textures; host
  image copy; sparse; external) report only the host-visible type, as
  do host-pointer imports.
- An image that can be private reports the larger size and alignment
  of its texture in a shared and in a private heap, so it fits either.
- Buffers keep every memory type (vkd3d-proton clears image memory with
  a buffer bound to it) and take the larger buffer alignment of a
  shared and a private heap.
- A buffer placed in a heap takes the heap's resource options (Metal
  requires the heap's storage mode).

Without the flag the memory types (one, host visible), every
requirement and every allocation are as before. The flag changes the
memory types an application sees, so it is in 0118's must-be-named
set: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=all alone does not turn it on.

Linear: PLA-541
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-08-vulkan-perf-private-memory.md;
 $PLAYPORT_BUILD/agent-notes/pla541/kk-sync-mem.md (finding 3),
 $PLAYPORT_BUILD/agent-notes/pla541/ev-kk-dxmt.md (private + compressible
 usage never run)
Offered-upstream: no (cf. mesa!44221, which adds the type but keeps its
 memory shared)
